apiVersion: v2
name: cracha
description: |
  Crachá issues AWS credentials to Kubernetes workloads from their SPIFFE
  identity. A pod's AWS SDK reads a short-lived JWT-SVID from a file and
  trades it with the broker for STS credentials; nothing in the pod changes.

  This chart installs the credential broker, the CSI node plugin that writes
  each pod's token, and the mutating webhook that wires opted-in pods up.
type: application
# The template of the chart's Chart.yaml: :chart_yaml writes @VERSION@ and
# @APP_VERSION@ from the workspace status (bazel/workspace_status.sh) at build
# time. Do not write a version here.
#
# A release, built from a commit tagged v<VERSION>, is versioned <VERSION>
# (or <VERSION>-rc.<n> for a candidate). Every other commit is a snapshot of
# the release it leads up to: <VERSION>-dev.<commit time, UTC>.g<commit>. The
# time makes snapshots order by age; the commit says what was built. The
# version being worked towards is the VERSION file at the root.
version: "@VERSION@"
appVersion: "@APP_VERSION@"
keywords:
  - aws
  - credentials
  - spiffe
  - csi
sources:
  - https://github.com/bpalermo/cracha
